{"schema_version":1,"source_commit":"100560de6c9f68c2875097d40a2012a84c784179","scope":"Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam Canto 2, Chapter 6 — Śrīdhara Svāmī word-for-word gloss","source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","entries":[{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":1,"end":1,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["षष्ठे","in the sixth [canto]"],["विराड्-विभूतिः","the opulences of the universal form"],["अध्यात्मादि-भेदतः","according to distinctions such as the individual and cosmic"],["पूर्वोक्तं सर्वम्","everything stated earlier"],["पुरुष-सूक्ततः दृढीकृतम्","is strengthened by the Puruṣa-sūkta"],["वाचाम्","of speech"],["अस्मद्-आदि-वाग्-इन्द्रियाणाम्","of the organ of speech, beginning with ours"],["तद्-अधिष्ठातुः वह्नेः","of Agni, its presiding deity"],["मुखं क्षेत्रम् उत्पत्ति-स्थानम्","the mouth is the field, the place of origin"],["गायत्र्य्-आदीनां सप्तानाम्","of the seven metres, beginning with Gāyatrī"],["सप्त-धातवः त्वग्-आदयः","the seven bodily constituents, beginning with skin"],["हव्यं देवानाम् अन्नम्","havis is the food of the gods"],["अमृतं तद्-उभय-शेषः मनुष्यानाम्","the remainder of both is amṛta for human beings"],["षड्-विधस्य सर्व-रसस्य","of all six kinds of taste"],["रसनेन्द्रियस्य अधिष्ठातुः वरुणस्य","of the tongue and its presiding deity, Varuṇa"],["जिह्वा क्षेत्रम् उत्पत्ति-स्थानम्","the tongue is the field, the place of origin"],["कव्यम्","an oblation offered to the ancestors"]],"note":"The source contains the doubtful form “पितृ-टणाम्” in the word for the ancestors; it is omitted rather than silently corrected."},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":2,"end":2,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["सर्वासूनाम्","of all living breaths"],["अस्मद्-आदि-प्राणानाम्","of the vital airs, beginning with ours"],["नासे नासारन्ध्रे","the nostrils, the openings of the nose"],["परमायने उत्तम-क्षेत्रे","the highest place, the excellent field"],["मोद-प्रमोदयोः","of delight and great delight"],["सामान्य-विशेष-गन्धयोः","of ordinary and distinctive scents"],["घ्राणः घ्राणेन्द्रियम्","smell means the sense of smell"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":3,"end":3,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["रूपाणां तेजसाम्","of forms and lights"],["रूप-प्रकाशानाम्","of visible manifestations"],["चक्षुर् इन्द्रियम्","the eye is the sense"],["अक्षिणी नेत्र-गोलके","the eyes are the eyeballs"],["षष्ठ्य्-अन्तानां प्रथमा-अन्तं क्षेत्रम्","for words in the genitive, supply the nominative ‘field’"],["कर्णौ श्रोत्र-अधिष्ठाने","the ears are the seats of hearing"],["श्रोत्रम् इन्द्रियम्","hearing is the sense"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":4,"end":4,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["गात्रं शरीरम्","the body"],["वस्तूनां ये सारांशाः","the essential parts of things"],["तेषां भाजनं स्थानम्","the vessel, the place for them"],["त्वक्-स्पर्शस्य वायोः च","of touch and of wind"],["सर्वस्य मेधस्य यज्ञस्य","of the entire sacrifice"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":5,"end":5,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["उद्भिज्ज-जातीनाम्","of the sprouting species"],["सर्व-वृक्षाणाम्","of all trees"],["यैर् वृक्षैर् यज्ञः सम्यक् साधितः","the trees by which a sacrifice is properly performed"],["केशाः मेघानाम् क्षेत्रम्","hair is the field of clouds"],["श्मश्रूणि विधुताम्","the moustache and beard belong to lightning"],["पाद-कर-नखानि शिलालोहानाम्","the nails of feet and hands belong to stones and metals"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":6,"end":6,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["क्षेम-कर्मणाम्","of the acts of preservation"],["पालन-कर्तॄणाम्","of those who protect"],["विक्रमः पादन्यासः","the stride is a step of the foot"],["भूर्-आदि-लोकानाम् आस्पदम् आश्रयः","the support of the worlds beginning with Bhūḥ"],["क्षेमः लब्ध-रक्षणम्","kṣema means protecting what has been gained"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":7,"end":7,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["शरणम्","shelter"],["भयाद् रक्षणम्","protection from fear"],["सर्वेषां कामानाम्","of all desires"],["हरेर् अङ्घ्रिर् आस्पदम्","Hari's feet are the refuge"],["वरस्य वरणस्य अपि","of the boon and of its choosing"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":8,"end":8,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["वीर्यस्य शुक्रस्य","of virility, semen"],["शिश्नः अधिष्ठानम्","the penis is the seat"],["उपस्थः तु इन्द्रियम्","the genital is the sense organ"],["प्रजात्य्-आनन्दः सन्तान-अर्थः सम्भोगः","sexual union, for the joy and purpose of offspring"],["निर्वृतिः ताप-हानिः","relief means the removal of distress"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":9,"end":9,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["परिमोक्षस्य मल-त्यागस्य","of release, the discharge of waste"],["पायुः इन्द्रियम्","the anus is the sense organ"],["गुदः स्थानम्","the rectum is its seat"],["निरृतेः अलक्ष्म्याः","of Nirṛti, misfortune"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":10,"end":10,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["तमसः अज्ञानस्य","of darkness, ignorance"],["पश्चिमः पृष्ठ-भागः","the back is the western side"],["गोत्राणाम् गिरीणाम्","of the lineages, the mountains"],["अस्थि-संघातः","the collection of bones"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":11,"end":11,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["अव्यक्तं प्रधानम्","the unmanifest is primordial matter"],["रसः अन्नादि-सारः","rasa is the essence of food and the like"],["सिन्धवः समुद्राः","the sindhus are the oceans"],["निधनस्य लयस्य","of dissolution"],["उदरं पदं स्थानम्","the belly is a place"],["मनसः अस्मद्-आदि-लिङ्ग-शरीरस्य","of the mind, the subtle body beginning with ours"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":12,"end":12,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["तुभ्यं तव","to you, your"],["कुमाराणां सनकादीनाम्","of the Kumāras, beginning with Sanaka"],["भवस्य श्री-रुद्रस्य","of Bhava, Śrī Rudra"],["आत्मा चित्तम्","the mind"],["परम् अयनम्","the highest refuge"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":13,"end":16,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["परमेश्वराज् जातं विश्वम्","the universe born from the Supreme Lord"],["ततो न भिन्नम्","is not separate from him"],["कुण्डलं सुवर्णात् न पृथक्","an earring is not separate from gold"],["सर्व-नियन्ता सर्व-प्रकाशकः","the ruler and illuminator of all"],["पुरुष-सूक्त-अर्थ-कथनेन","by explaining the meaning of the Puruṣa-sūkta"],["सहस्र-शीर्षा इति","with the words ‘thousand-headed’"],["पुरुष एव इदं सर्वम्","the Person alone is all this"],["अहं भवान्","I and you"],["ते तव अग्रजाः","these are your elder brothers"],["सनकादयः मरीच्य्-आदयः च","Sanaka and the others, and Marīci and the others"],["जलं स्थलं नभः च","water, land and sky"],["नभौकसः","those whose home is the sky"],["सर्वम् इदं पुरुष एव","all this is the Person alone"],["न ततः पृथक्","not separate from him"],["विश्वम् भूमि-पदस्य अर्थः","the universe is the meaning of ‘earth’"],["आवृतम् वृत्वा","having enveloped, having covered"],["अनुपयोगात् अपरिच्छिन्नत्वात् च","because measurement is inapplicable and he is unlimited"]],"note":"The Śrīdhara commentary treats 2.6.13–16 together while explaining the Puruṣa-sūkta; the grouped range is retained."},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":17,"end":17,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["असौ प्राणः आदित्यः","that vital breath is the sun"],["असौ वा आदित्यः प्राणः","or that sun is vital breath"],["स्व-धिष्ण्यं मण्डलम्","its own sphere"],["बहिः च प्रकाशयति","it illuminates outside as well"],["विराड्-देहं प्रकाशयन्","illuminating the universal body"],["ब्रह्माण्डम् अन्तर्-बहिः प्रकाशयति","it illumines the universe inside and out"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":18,"end":18,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["नित्यम् उक्तत्वम्","the statement that he is eternal"],["अभयस्य","of fearlessness"],["मन्त्र-गत-अमृत-पद-व्याख्या","the explanation of ‘immortality’ in the mantra"],["अन्नेन इति पदम्","the word ‘by food’"],["विभक्ति-व्यत्ययेन","by changing the grammatical case"],["मर्त्यं मरण-धर्मकम्","mortal, subject to death"],["अन्नं कर्म-फलम्","food means the fruit of action"],["सर्वात्मकः","the Self of all"],["अमृतत्वस्य निज-आनन्दस्य ईश्वरः","the Lord of immortality, his own bliss"],["महिमा विभूतिः","glory means opulence"],["ज्यायान् महत्तरः","greater, exceedingly great"]],"note":"The source reads the doubtful form “अतिक्वान्तवान्”; this word is omitted rather than silently changed."},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":19,"end":19,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["ईश्वरः नित्य-मुक्तः","the Lord is eternally liberated"],["तद्-आश्रितानां भूतानाम्","of beings who depend on him"],["बन्ध-मोक्षौ व्यवस्थया","bondage and liberation, according to order"],["भूर्-आदि-लोकाः स्थितयः","the worlds beginning with Bhūḥ are abodes"],["ते पादाः इव अंशाः यस्य","they are like feet, portions of him"],["स्थिति-पात्","the support of all abodes"],["पादेषु अंश-भूतेषु लोकेषु","in the worlds that are portions of his feet"],["त्रिपाद् अमृतं नित्य-सुखम्","the three quarters are immortality, eternal bliss"],["दिवि ऊर्ध्व-लोकेषु","in the heavenly worlds above"],["न त्रिलोक्याम्","not in the three worlds"],["महर्-लोकः मूर्धा","Maharloka is the head"],["जन-लोकादिषु","in Janaloka and the worlds above"],["त्रिलोक्यां नश्वरम् एव सुखम्","happiness in the three worlds is perishable"],["सत्य-लोके अभयं मोक्षः","in Satyaloka there is fearlessness, liberation"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":20,"end":20,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["अधिकारि-भेदेन","according to differences in eligibility"],["न प्रजायन्ते","they do not beget offspring"],["अप्रजाः","those without progeny"],["नैष्ठिक-ब्रह्मचारि-वान-प्रस्थ-यतयः","lifelong celibates, forest-dwellers and renunciants"],["तेषाम् आश्रमाः","their stages of life"],["त्रिलोक्याः बहिः आसन्","were outside the three worlds"],["गृह-मेधः तु अन्तः","the householder's wisdom is within"],["अबृहद्-व्रतः","one without the great vow of celibacy"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":21,"end":21,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["अवस्था-भेदेन","by differences of state"],["न तु अत्यन्त-भिन्न-विषयः","not as a completely different subject"],["विष्वङ् पुरुषः क्षेत्र-ज्ञः","the all-pervading Person, the knower of the field"],["सृती मार्गौ दक्षिण-उत्तरौ","the two paths, southern and northern"],["विचक्रमे चलति स्म","he traversed"],["साशन-अनशने","with and without food"],["भोग-अपवर्ग-प्राप्ति-साधन-भूते","which are means for enjoyment and liberation"],["अविद्या कर्म-रूपा एका","one is ignorance in the form of action"],["विद्या तत्-साधन-उपासना-रूपा अन्या","the other is knowledge in the form of worship, its means"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":22,"end":22,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["विराड्-अन्तर्वर्तिनाम्","of those within the universal form"],["फल-वैचित्र्यम्","the variety of results"],["तत्-कारण-ईश्वरस्य","of the Lord, the cause of them"],["यस्माद् अण्डं जज्ञे","from whom the universe was born"],["भूतेन्द्रिय-गुणात्मकः विराट्","the universal form consists of elements, senses and qualities"],["स ईश्वरः","that Lord"],["विश्वं विराड्-देहं द्रव्यम् अण्डं च","the universe, the universal body and the material shell"],["अतिक्रान्तवान्","he transcended"],["सूर्य इव","like the sun"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":23,"end":23,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["यज्ञस्य तत्-साधनानां च","of sacrifice and its means"],["अ-पृथग्-भावात्","because they are not separate"],["यज्ञैः पुरुष-आराधनम्","worship of the Person through sacrifices"],["न सिध्येत्","would not be possible"],["यज्ञस्य सम्भारान् साधनानि","the materials and means of sacrifice"],["न अपश्यम्","I did not see"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":24,"end":24,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["सम्भारेषु साध्येषु सत्सु","when the sacrificial materials had been gathered"],["पुरुष-अवयवैः","through the limbs of the Person"],["एते सम्भाराः सम्भृताः","these materials were assembled"],["वनस्पतयः यूपाः","trees are the sacrificial posts"],["देव-यजनं यज्ञ-भूमिः","the place of worship is the sacrificial ground"],["यज्ञ-अर्हे स्थाने","in a place suitable for sacrifice"],["वसन्तादि-कालः","the season beginning with spring"],["बहु-गुण-अन्वितः","endowed with many qualities"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":25,"end":25,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["वस्तूनि पात्र-आदीनि","objects such as the sacrificial vessels"],["ओषधयः व्रीह्य्-आदयः","plants, such as rice and the rest"],["स्नेहाः घृत-आदयः","unctuous substances, such as ghee"],["रसाः मधुर-आदयः","flavors, beginning with sweetness"],["सुवर्ण-आदीनि लोहानि","metals such as gold"],["मृदः च जलं च","clay and water"],["चातुर्होत्रं","the four kinds of priestly service"],["होत्रादिकं कर्म","rites beginning with the Hotṛ's work"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":26,"end":26,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["नामधेयानि","the ritual names"],["ज्योतिष्टोम-आदीनि","such as Jyotiṣṭoma"],["मन्त्राः","mantras"],["स्वाहा-कार-आदयः","the utterances beginning with ‘svāhā’"],["देवतानाम् अनुक्रमः उद्देशः","the list of deities is their enumeration"],["कल्पः","the ritual procedure"],["बौधायनादि-कर्म-पद्धति-ग्रन्थः","a manual of ritual, such as Baudhāyana's"],["अनेन अहं यक्ष्य इति संकल्पः","the resolve ‘by this I shall sacrifice’"],["तन्त्रम् अनुष्ठान-प्रकारः","tantra is the method of performance"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":27,"end":27,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["गतयः","the courses"],["विष्णु-क्रम-आद्याः","beginning with the steps of Viṣṇu"],["मतयः","the meditations"],["देवत-ध्यानानि","meditations on deities"],["कृतस्य भगवति समर्पणम्","offering to Bhagavān what has been done"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":28,"end":28,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["सम्भृताः सम्पादिताः","assembled, prepared"],["सम्भाराः येन सः अहम्","I, by whom the materials were collected"],["तेन एव यज्ञेन एव","by that very sacrifice"],["यज्ञेन यज्ञम् अयजन्त","they worshiped the sacrifice by sacrifice"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":29,"end":29,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["तेन देवा अयजन्त","the gods worshiped by him"],["स-प्रपञ्चम्","in detail"],["व्यक्तम् इन्द्रादि-रूपेण","manifest in forms beginning with Indra"],["अव्यक्तं स्वतः","unmanifest in itself"],["पुरुषं जातम् अग्रतः","the Person born at the beginning"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":30,"end":30,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["काले स्व-स्व-अवसरे","at the proper time for each"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":31,"end":31,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["यद्-अधिष्ठानम्","that which is the substratum"],["प्रश्नोत्तरार्थम् उपसंहरति","he concludes the question and answer"],["आहितम् अधिष्ठितम्","placed, established"],["सर्गादौ","at the beginning of creation"],["मायया गृहीताः","assumed through māyā"],["उरवो गुणाः","the powerful qualities"]],"note":"The pinned source reads “स्वतोऽगुणह्”, a damaged ending in the gloss. That token is omitted instead of being silently normalized."},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":32,"end":32,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["यत् परः त्वम्","you who are supreme"],["प्रश्नोत्तरम् उपसंहरति","he concludes the answer"],["सृजामि इति","with the word ‘I create’"],["पालनं तु स्वयम् एव करोति","he himself performs maintenance"],["पुरुष-रूपेण विष्णु-रूपेण","in the form of the Person, in Viṣṇu's form"],["त्रि-शक्तिः माया","the threefold power is māyā"],["तां धरति","he bears it"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":33,"end":33,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["सामान्य-उत्तरम्","the general answer"],["पुरुष एव इदं सर्वम्","the Person alone is all this"],["सद्-असद्-आत्मकम्","consisting of cause and effect"],["भाव्यं सृज्यम्","what is to be created"],["भगवतः सकाशात्","from Bhagavān"],["अन्यत् पृथक् न भवति","nothing else exists separately"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":34,"end":34,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["यद् यस्मात्","that, because"],["मे मया","from me, by me"],["औत्कण्ठ्यं भक्त्य्-उद्रेकः","eagerness means an increase of devotion"],["तद्-युक्तेन हृदा","with a heart filled with it"],["हरिर् धृतो ध्यातः","Hari is held in mind, meditated upon"],["अङ्ग हे नारद","O dear Nārada"],["वाङ्-मन-इन्द्रियाणां वृत्तयः सत्यार्थाः","the activities of my speech, mind and senses convey the truth"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":35,"end":35,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["स्व-अनुभवम्","his own experience"],["अन्वय-व्यतिरेकाभ्याम्","by presence and absence"],["प्रमाणयति","he demonstrates"],["समाम्नायादिभिः सर्वोत्कृष्टः अपि","although supreme through the Veda and the rest"],["योगम् आश्रित्य अपि","even having resorted to yoga"],["आत्मनः मम सम्भवः जन्म","the origin, my own birth"],["तम् एव न ज्ञातवान्","I did not know it"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":36,"end":36,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["समीयुषाम् शरणागतानाम्","of those who have approached for shelter"],["भवच्-छिदम् संसार-निवर्तकम्","that which cuts worldly existence"],["सुमङ्गलं मङ्गलावहम्","very auspicious, bringing good fortune"],["सुसेव्यम्","easy to serve"],["तस्य चरणं नतः अस्मि","I bow to his feet"],["स्व-माया-विस्तारम्","the extent of his own māyā"],["पर्यगात्","he has completely traversed"],["परि-शब्दः निषेधे","the particle pari conveys negation"],["अपरे कुतः जानीयुः","how could others know?"],["स्वस्यान्तं नभः न आप्नोति","the sky does not reach its own limit"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":37,"end":37,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["वामदेवः रुद्रः","Vāmadeva is Rudra"],["ऋतां गतिम्","the course of truth"],["परमार्थ-स्वरूपम्","the nature of the highest reality"],["प्रपञ्च-रूपम्","in the form of the universe"],["मायया विनिर्मितम्","fashioned by māyā"],["विचक्ष्महे विद्मः","we discern, we know"],["आत्म-समम् स्व-ज्ञान-अनुरूपम्","corresponding to our own knowledge"],["न तु कृत्स्नम्","but not in its entirety"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":38,"end":38,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["सर्वेऽपि तं वर्णयन्तः","although everyone appears to describe him"],["दृश्यन्ते","they are seen"],["तत्र आह","he answers that"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":39,"end":39,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["अवतार-कर्माणि","the acts of the incarnations"],["संक्षेपतः दर्शयति","he summarizes"],["आद्यः भगवान्","the original Bhagavān"],["पुरुष-अवतारः सन्","being the Puruṣa incarnation"],["सृष्ट्य्-आदि करोति","he performs creation and the rest"],["कर्ता अधिकरणं साधनं कर्म","the agent, location, instrument and action"],["स्वयम् एव","himself alone"],["संक्षेप-उक्तिः","a concise statement"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":40,"end":40,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["ज्ञानं केवलं सत्यम् तत्त्वम्","knowledge alone is the true reality"],["विशुद्धम् विषय-आकार-शून्यम्","pure, free of the forms of objects"],["प्रत्यक् सर्वान्तरम्","inward, within all"],["सम्यक् सन्देहादि-रहितम्","complete, free from doubt and the rest"],["अवस्थितं स्थिरम्","established, steady"],["निर्गुणम्","beyond the qualities"],["अनादि-अन्तम् जन्म-नाश-रहितम्","without beginning or end, free from birth and death"],["वृद्धि-विपरिणाम-अपक्षयाः न सन्ति","there is no growth, transformation or decline"],["पूर्णम्","complete"],["नित्यम् अद्वयम्","eternal and nondual"],["परमार्थतः अद्वयम्","ultimately nondual even when duality appears"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":41,"end":41,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["विद्वद्-अनुभवम् प्रमाणयति","he establishes it through the experience of the wise"],["प्रशान्त-आत्म-इन्द्रिय-आशयाः","those whose mind, senses and heart are peaceful"],["प्रसन्न-देह-इन्द्रिय-मनसः","whose body, senses and mind are serene"],["यदा भवन्ति","when they become"],["तदा विदन्ति","then they know"],["तर्कैर् विप्लुतम्","pervaded by arguments"],["तदा तिरोधीयते","then it disappears from view"]],"note":"The source addresses Nārada as “ऋसे”, a doubtful form; the WFW omits it rather than silently changing it to “ऋषे”."},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":42,"end":42,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["अवतारान् विस्तरेण आह","he explains the incarnations in detail"],["परस्य भूम्नः पुरुषः","the Puruṣa of the Supreme, the All-pervading"],["प्रकृति-प्रवर्तकः","the one who sets material nature in motion"],["सहस्र-शीर्षा इति उक्तः","described as ‘thousand-headed’"],["लीला-विग्रहः","the form assumed for pastimes"],["आद्यः अवतारः","the first incarnation"],["कालः स्वभावः सद्-असत्","time, nature, cause and effect"],["मनो महत्-तत्त्वम्","manas means the mahat principle"],["द्रव्यं महा-भूतानि","substance means the great elements"],["विकारोऽहंकारः","transformation means ahaṅkāra"],["गुणः सत्त्वादिः","guṇa means sattva and the rest"],["विराट् समष्टि-शरीरम्","Virāṭ is the collective body"],["स्वराट् वैराजः","Svarāṭ is the cosmic ruler"],["स्थास्नु स्थावरम् चरिष्णु जङ्गमम्","sthāsnu means stationary, cariṣṇu means moving"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":43,"end":43,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["अहं ब्रह्मा","aham means Brahmā"],["भवः रुद्रः","Bhava means Rudra"],["यज्ञः विष्णुः","Yajña means Viṣṇu"],["दक्षादयः","Dakṣa and the others"],["प्रजेशाः","the lords of creation"],["तल-लोक-पालाः पाताल-अधिपतयः","the guardians of the lower worlds, lords of Pātāla"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":44,"end":44,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["गन्धर्वादीनाम् ईशाः","the lords of the Gandharvas and others"],["यक्षादीनां नाथाः","the masters of the Yakṣas and others"],["ऋषीणां पितॄणां च श्रेष्ठाः","the foremost among sages and ancestors"],["प्रेतादीनाम् अधीशाः","the rulers of ghosts and the rest"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":45,"end":45,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["यत् किंचिद् भगवद्-आदि","whatever begins with Bhagavān"],["तत् सर्वं परम् एव तत्त्वम्","all of that is the supreme reality"],["भगवद् ऐश्वर्य-युक्तम्","endowed with the Lord's majesty"],["महस्वत् तेजो-युक्तम्","possessing radiance and splendor"],["ओजः-सहसी इन्द्रिय-मनः-शक्ती","ojas and sahas are powers of the senses and mind"],["बलं दाक्ष्यम्","bala means skill"],["श्रीः शोभा ह्रीः अकर्म-जुगुप्सा","śrī means beauty; hrī means aversion to improper action"],["विभूतिः संपत्तिः आत्मा बुद्धिः","vibhūti means wealth; ātman means intelligence"],["अर्णः वर्णः","arṇa means color"],["अद्भुत-अर्णम् आश्चर्य-वर्णम्","of a wondrous color"],["रूपम् एव स्वरूपम्","form itself is essential nature"],["रूपवत् अस्वरूपम् च","and that which is not the essential form, though possessing form"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":6,"start":46,"end":46,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/06_virATsvarUpam.md","source_blob_sha":"8a7846b129aa7510cbf69679b413568e238af1ab","pairs":[["शुद्ध-सत्त्व-अवतारान्","the incarnations of pure goodness"],["असत्-कथा-श्रवणैः","by hearing unworthy stories"],["कर्णयोः कषायाः मलाः","the impurities in the ears"],["तान् शोषयन्ति","they dry them up"],["सुपेशान् सुन्दरान्","beautiful, very lovely"],["स-कार-लोपः आर्षः","the loss of the syllable sa is Vedic usage"],["ते तुभ्यम् अनुक्रमिष्ये","I shall recount them to you in order"],["तद्-अनुक्रमेण","in that sequence"],["पीयताम्","let it be drunk"],["कर्ण-कषाय-शोषान्","the purifier of impurities in the ears"]]}]}